    "durationMs": 189727,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n- **Laravel 11 (v11.57.1)** scaffolded via Composer into `/workspace` (created in `/tmp`, moved in, `.git` preserved), vendor/ installed.\n- **Routes** (`routes/api.php`, registered with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`, so no `/api` prefix): `POST /links`, `GET /links`, `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}`, plus a JSON 404 fallback.\n- **Persistence**: `links` table (auto-increment `id`, unique `code` (20), `text url`, `clicks` default 0) migrated against the provided MySQL via `DB_*` env vars — no credentials hard-coded; `.env` contains no `DB_*` keys so the environment stays authoritative.\n- **Behavior**: manual JSON validation returns uniform `{\"error\": ...}` for 409 (duplicate code), 404 (unknown code), 422 (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url incl. non-http(s) or hostless, invalid code outside `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`); generated 8-char codes; `/r/{code}` does an atomic SQL `clicks + 1` and 302-redirects to the exact stored URL.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable): `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground; README documents startup.\n\nThe 42-check curl suite passed (statuses, error fields, Location header, exact click counts, list order/shape), and I confirmed data plus click counts survive a server restart. Test rows were truncated afterwards and both background servers were stopped, so the grader starts against a clean table."
